			"widgets_values":[
				"Ma Xiaoxiong's artistic style features vertical compositions with low-angle shots looking up, and cinematic color grading. A bustling pedestrian street where traditional Chinese upturned eaves blend with cyberpunk skyscrapers, the buildings covered in pink neon signs and electronic screen ads (neon signs grouped into large readable shapes, text labels clear and controlled, without spreading into dirty texture clusters), under a deep night sky. The asphalt is wet and reflective (strict dry-wet boundaries, matte asphalt absorbs light, shallow puddles have controlled mirror reflections, no global wetness). Scattered, small pedestrians move through (a few readable silhouettes, not a dense crowd); street-side trees are irregularly spaced, floating mechanical lamp posts and trendy cyber text signs add to the scene. High-saturation neon clash (accent colors do not bleed or mix), intertwined cold and warm lighting, giving a strong sense of lively urban nightlife. Dark-toned, high-end night scene ambiance, transparent volumetric light diffusion (controlled layers, strict boundaries, near solid/far soft, not diffused into global haze). Surfaces: wet asphalt (strict dry-wet boundaries, porous matte absorbing dry areas, reflections adjusted for puddle distance and roughness, no milky mirror), Chinese upturned eaves (matte tiles, wear only on exposed edges, grazing light reveals tile textures), cyberpunk glass façades (roughness variation, controlled reflections only where physically triggered, no milky reflection), pink neon signs and screens (self-illuminated controlled highlights, strict boundaries, large readable shape groupings, no degrading to repeated tiny patterns), pedestrian silhouettes (dark-toned, edge light separates figure from neon background), trees (matte leaves, controlled rim light), floating mechanical lamps (matte metal, narrow anisotropic highlights on worn edges). Neon light is main light, pink warm light clashes with blue cool light, volumetric light penetrates haze creating Tyndall beams (layered and controlled), grazing light reveals puddle surfaces and tiled eaves textures. Under high-saturation neon, road, buildings, neon, and pedestrians are distinguished by roughness, highlight width, color temperature, and edge response, not new colors. Protected highlight textures, smooth cinematic highlight transitions, readable shadow bases, local contact shadows only at pedestrians’ feet, tree roots and eave joints, no dirty AO glow. Air perspective recedes, distant scenery blends into controlled fog. Clean rendering, balanced details, focus on the intersection of upward-looking eaves and neon signs, only natural textures, controlled material rendering, clean gradients, controlled highlights, minimal repeating patterns, large readable shape groupings, multilayered media control, frosted matte surfaces, neon text clearly controlled. Avoid: milky global reflections, full-scene wetness, repeating micro-pattern noise, dirty texture accumulation, random small symbols, watermark-like marks, stray text or watermarks (except neon signs), uniform chrome gloss, plastic gallery look, dirty AO halos, global haze, crushed blacks or highlights, accent color bleeding, dense crowds, objects merging into plastic-like blobs, uniform roughness or highlight width, black edges on every object, dirty ink residues, ghost textures, pseudo-shadows, low contrast leftover textures."
			],
